{
    "title": "phplyr backends and dplyr",
    "description": "Three pipelines on a generated sales table of 100,000 and 1,000,000 rows, joined to a 100-row store table. phplyr runs each on phibble's in-memory DataFrame, on PolarsTable (Polars at 2 threads), and on SQLite through SqlTable. dplyr runs the first two pipelines on the same data. The pipeline with a PHP closure has no dplyr version. Every backend returned the same rows as DataFrame, and dplyr's row counts and column sums matched.",
